AIM
The aim of this experiment is to study Wireshark – a network protocol analyzer used for packet capture, analysis, and network troubleshooting. The study includes installation, packet capture, packet analysis, filtering, and use of statistics tools.

Problem Statement
Install Wireshark on a Windows or Linux system.
Capture live network traffic using Wireshark (GUI and command line).
Apply capture and display filters to isolate specific traffic.
Analyze captured packets and identify protocols, source/destination addresses, and payload content.
Use Wireshark's statistics and analysis tools to understand network traffic patterns.
Save and open capture files for offline analysis.
Input
Live network interface with internet connectivity
(Optional) Pre‑saved capture file (.pcap or .pcapng)
Output
Captured packets displayed in the Wireshark GUI
Filtered traffic based on user‑defined criteria
Statistics reports (Protocol Hierarchy, Endpoints, Conversations)
Saved capture file for offline analysis
